{"content":[{"c":["JEHOSHEBA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Daughter of King Jehoram of Judah (853–841 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") and Queen Athaliah, sister of King Ahaziah (841 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), and wife of Jehoiada the high priest. Upon Ahaziah’s death, Athaliah attempted to kill all the remaining royal heirs to the throne; Jehosheba, however, hid young Joash, Ahaziah’s son, in a temple bedroom for the duration of Athaliah’s reign (841–835 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.11.2","r":"2Kgs.11.2","rawR":"2Kgs.11.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.11.2","value":"2Kgs.11.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 11:2"},"). Jehosheba is alternately spelled Jehoshabeath in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.22.11","r":"2Chr.22.11","rawR":"2Chr.22.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.22.11","value":"2Chr.22.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chronicles 22:11"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Jehosheba","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 11:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.11.2","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.11.2","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.11.2"},{"anchorText":"2 Chronicles 22:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.22.11","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.22.11","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.22.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d383a8afe8873545cc8b39a958433dfb759cc6a0af082b5e1b1cd82b09d2b2a7","sourceItemName":"Jehosheba","sourceItemOrder":157,"sourceMember":"Articles/J.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Jehosheba","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Jehosheba","title":"Jehosheba","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}